{"timestamp":"2026-08-23T16:19:21.155Z","ordinal":15528,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a02f6b-5fc3-77e2-b29e-16e655e520f4","call_id":"call_0wwjtxOXCFi40fcIF0xhx7qJ","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/phase2_gatekeeper\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"Phase 2 gatekeeper findings for `/root`:\\n\\nCurrent baseline is healthy but still Phase 1:\\n\\n- `internal/cli/distill_candidates.go:1237-1295` explicitly emits one card per batch; `CandidateIDs` is always singleton. The packer sorts by source identity/line/id, not session creation time.\\n- `internal/cli/distill_cmd.go:2116-2183` fingerprints/render-chunks the whole session candidate input; there is no per-member extraction cache.\\n- `internal/cli/distill_cmd.go:1160-1270` executes one provider call per chunk. Candidate mode skips reconciliation via `newDistilledFactActions`, but output parsing does not yet enforce candidate-ID attribution.\\n- `internal/cli/distill_cmd.go:512-518` remains a session-level cache. The candidate namespace only prevents legacy cache collisions; it is not v2 staged cache state.\\n- Existing candidate tests pass: `go test ./internal/cli -run 'Test(Distill|Candidate)' -count=1`.\\n\\nRecommended fixed packing MVP:\\n\\n- Sort by `(session CreatedAt, session ID, turn/source line, candidate ID)`.\\n- Keep repository identity as a hard pack key; never mix repos.\\n- First-fit sequential packing, no backtracking or dynamic tuning.\\n- Fixed rendered pack cap: `32 KiB`; fixed member cap: `32`.\\n- Keep each card intact; enforce the plan’s 8 KiB hard card ceiling, refusing a card whose complete trigger cannot fit.\\n- With the measured 1,415,420 candidate bytes / 368 cards, this predicts roughly 45 calls (`ceil(bytes / 32 KiB)`), within the 30–60 target. Treat this as one predeclared policy; do not tune pack size repeatedly against one local run.\\n\\n| Area | Phase 2 acceptance blocker | Evidence/seam |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Protocol quality | Define exact framed output, e.g. `candidate_id<TAB>NO_FACTS` or `candidate_id<TAB>kind<TAB>path<TAB>fact`. Every expected member must appear exactly once as sentinel or fact; unknown/duplicate/missing IDs invalidate the pack and never cache emptiness. | Prompt extension currently only describes IDs (`distill.go:21-52`); parser currently accepts unframed lines (`distill.go:305-337`). |\\n| Attribution | Strip candidate ID before existing fact parsing; provenance must use the member’s anchor, never the pack anchor. Add tests for cross-member misattribution and omitted IDs. | `distill_cmd.go:1160-1205`; `distilledFactsFromOutput` in `distill.go:223-302`. |\\n| Deterministic performance | Fixed 32 KiB first-fit packing produces measured 30–60 calls, no reconcile calls, and ≥80% fewer extraction calls than 64 KiB legacy / ≥90% fewer total calls than legacy extraction+reconcile upper bound. | Current measured target is documented in `docs/candidate_distillation_plan.md` Stage 3 and gates. |\\n| Failure isolation | On provider/protocol failure, bisect once into deterministic halves. Never mark any member successful/empty from a failed parent pack. Successful member cache entries survive repacking; failed members remain uncached. No recursive retry loop. | New seam belongs around `preparedSession.result` / current worker dispatch (`distill_cmd.go:148-159`, `350-386`). |\\n| Member cache | Key by redacted card digest + extraction prompt version + taxonomy digest + agent command/model/effort. Exclude branch, transcript path/line, packing policy, and confidence. Cache successful empty output and facts; never cache failure. | Current session cache/salt: `distill_cmd.go:512-518`, `2340-2400`; v2 layout required by plan. |\\n| Shadow/no-write | Phase 2 must invoke candidate extraction but not mutate active facts, proposals, or the active facts manifest. Compare candidate and legacy outputs using the same cutoff/model/prompt/taxonomy and retained labels. A dry-run alone is insufficient because it makes no calls. | Current `--dry-run` exits before execution (`distill_cmd.go:707-716`); normal candidate execution writes facts (`1160-1270`). Add explicit shadow path or isolated shadow store. |\\n| Usage accounting | Report pack calls, retries/splits, member cache hits/misses, provider-reported input/output/cache/reasoning tokens, missing usage, and wall time. Do not multiply pack usage across members; any per-member allocation must be explicitly estimated. | Existing provider collector is aggregate-only (`distill_usage.go:19-121`), and source publication persists usage at `distill_cmd.go:1354-1359`. |\\n| Privacy | Candidate metadata contains no plaintext. Redacted member results/fact text receive fact-store permissions and lifecycle. Excluded sessions are filtered before planning/cache lookup; purge must remove or conservatively invalidate v2 member state. A whole-v2-cache reset is acceptable for Phase 2 correctness; selective survivor recomputation is later optimization. | Egress/privacy lock and tombstone filtering already exist (`distill_cmd.go:777-786`, `839-843`). Purge currently only resets legacy cache (`session_privacy.go:1678-1692`); inventory recognizes only legacy cache/temp paths (`1520-1533`). Extend `sessionPurgePlan`/cleanup (`885-924`, `1837-1911`) and add bundle exclusion coverage. |\\n| Determinism | Same cards produce byte-identical packs/results independent of input order, concurrency, branch replay, or packing policy. Materialization order remains chronological even when calls complete out of order. | Current candidate ID stability tests exist; cross-session pack ordering must be added. |\\n\\nMust-have Phase 2 tests:\\n\\n- Multi-card framing: all-member sentinels, fact attribution, unknown/duplicate/missing IDs.\\n- Deterministic 32 KiB packing, repository separation, card-size refusal, 368-card call-count benchmark.\\n- One failed pack → two retries; no failure cached; successful neighbors retained.\\n- Cache reuse after repacking, concurrency change, branch replay, transcript relocation; model/prompt/taxonomy invalidation only at extraction layer.\\n- Shadow proves zero active fact/proposal/manifest mutation.\\n- Provider usage complete/partial/missing and retry accounting.\\n- Tombstone/exclude/purge, permissions, no plaintext cache, bundle exclusion, corrupt-cache rebuild.\\n- Paired legacy/candidate quality on the gold corpus: candidate span recall ≥95% overall and ≥98% for direct human rules/preferences/revisions/closed negatives; candidate fact recall non-inferior within 2 percentage points; no review-only active facts; every emitted fact supported by its member span.\\n\\nDefer beyond Phase 2:\\n\\n- Opt-in fact writes and reconciliation (Phase 3).\\n- Safe paraphrase merging; stay exact-only until 99% labeled precision.\\n- Automatic supersession; MVP must queue all different-ID relationships.\\n- Session-end hook routing and incremental append optimization (Phase 4).\\n- Default rollout, manifest schema changes, selective cache survivor pruning, and pack-size/provider-specific tuning (Phase 5/later).\\n\\nRecommended stop/reassess checkpoints:\\n\\n1. **P2a — protocol + packer:** run unit/integration tests and deterministic synthetic packing benchmark. If framing or bisection is unstable, stop before cache work.\\n2. **P2b — shadow corpus:** run one fixed-policy full labeled-corpus comparison. Judge quality first, then call/tokens/latency. If quality misses, fix admission/framing rather than optimizing pack size.\\n3. **P2c — cache/privacy/usage:** verify no-op, append, model/prompt invalidation, purge, and usage completeness. Only after this should Phase 2 be considered complete and Phase 3 writes discussed.\\n\\nAvoid local optimization loops by freezing the 32 KiB policy, running one retained benchmark per checkpoint, and recording misses as evidence rather than repeatedly changing thresholds or pack size.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/phase2_member_cache\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"Completed the standalone per-candidate cache primitive and tests.\\n\\n- Files: `internal/cli/distill_cache_v2.go`, `internal/cli/distill_cache_v2_test.go`\\n- Deterministic, bounded, atomic single-file NDJSON cache.\\n- Success-only results: explicit empty or canonical redacted facts.\\n- Identity covers required extraction inputs and excludes packing/provenance/confidence fields.\\n- Retains session ID plus ownership digest for future tombstone purging.\\n- Verification: `go test ./internal/cli -count=1` passed.\\n\\nIntegration and privacy-inventory wiring remain intentionally separate.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/phase2_protocol\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"Phase-2 protocol work is complete and reported to the parent agent.\\n\\n- Pure typed parser with atomic multi-member validation\\n- V2 candidate-ID prompt contract, with V1 preserved\\n- Per-candidate six-fact cap; no pack-wide cap\\n- Focused and full CLI tests passed before handoff; latest focused suite passes after concurrent integration edits.\"}}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a02f65-7c17-7a30-9a2a-f255f8bc2ae4"}}}
