{"timestamp":"2026-08-23T16:39:30.878Z","ordinal":16052,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a02f7d-d53e-7623-ac44-a9ee3c742d52","author":"/root/phase2_runtime_review","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/phase2_runtime_review\nPayload:\nNo HIGH blockers found.\n\nMEDIUM blockers:\n\n1. Split retries bypass the configured global concurrency cap, and reported capacity becomes false.\n   - [distill_shadow_v2.go](/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-brain/internal/cli/distill_shadow_v2.go:215) releases the failed parent’s semaphore slot at line 188, allowing the dispatcher to start another normal pack, then invokes each bisection child directly at line 221 outside that semaphore. A `--concurrency=4` run can therefore have four prefetched requests plus one retry request concurrently.\n   - The summary still reports `ExtractionJobsCap` based only on initial packs at [line 275](/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-brain/internal/cli/distill_shadow_v2.go:275), hiding the overage.\n   - This violates the plan’s “dispatch packs concurrently under existing `--concurrency` limit” requirement and makes rate-limit/performance evidence unreliable. Route split calls through the same pool/semaphore (or acquire its slot explicitly) and report the actual cap.\n\n2. Cross-session packing is not globally canonical for equal creation timestamps.\n   - Live execution sorts only by `CreatedAt` at [distill_cmd.go:886](/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-brain/internal/cli/distill_cmd.go:886); dry-run repeats the same under-specified sort at [line 1785](/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-brain/internal/cli/distill_cmd.go:1785).\n   - Shadow then retains that order while building the global member sequence at [distill_shadow_v2.go:72](/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-brain/internal/cli/distill_shadow_v2.go:72).\n   - The plan requires session creation time, session ID, then source turn ordering. Stable sort preserves whatever manifest ordering happens to arrive for timestamp ties, changing pack membership/request context and hence shadow measurements across equivalent corpus exports. Add deterministic tie-breakers before packing.\n\n3. Shadow dry-run relabels admitted candidate cards as cache misses.\n   - [distill_cmd.go:1495](/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-brain/internal/cli/distill_cmd.go:1495) correctly computes predicted extraction calls from miss packs, but [line 1496](/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-brain/internal/cli/distill_cmd.go:1496) overwrites `CandidateCards` with `candidateCacheMisses`.\n   - A fully cached corpus therefore reports zero `candidate_cards` despite admitting cards; live shadow reports all admitted cards at [distill_shadow_v2.go:260](/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-brain/internal/cli/distill_shadow_v2.go:260).\n   - This breaks dry-run/live funnel parity and the plan’s required candidate-card versus extraction-cache accounting. Keep admitted-card count separate from member misses.\n\nAssessment: shadow isolation looks sound: active facts, manifest, taxonomy, proposals, and v1 cache are not written; only the isolated v2 member cache is persisted. Per-member success/empty caching, protocol atomicity, one-level bisection, cancellation/join structure, and total call/token counting otherwise look coherent. Phase 1/legacy paths remain separated. Focused race tests passed:\n\n`go test -race ./internal/cli -run 'TestCandidateShadowV2|TestDistillCandidate.*V2|TestCandidate.*(Pack|Protocol|Cache)' -count=1`\n\nPhase 2 is substantively close, but the three medium issues block trustworthy concurrency-bound performance evidence, deterministic global packing, and complete dry-run accounting required by `docs/candidate_distillation_plan.md`."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a02f65-7c17-7a30-9a2a-f255f8bc2ae4"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-23T16:39:37.495Z","ordinal":16053,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a0200a-63d8-7b21-adef-c3850aecebf7","turn_id":"01a02f65-7c17-7a30-9a2a-f255f8bc2ae4","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0873a68aa02aff8f016a8b2248349081988242f9e6f9498745","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The first independent reviews are in: privacy/security is clean, while runtime found three bounded Phase 2 issues—retry concurrency, deterministic tie ordering, and dry-run card accounting. I’m fixing exactly those contract gaps, then I’ll rerun the fixed-policy performance check and a small real-model quality smoke."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1787503176180,"completed_at_ms":1787503177495}}
