{"timestamp":"2026-08-23T16:40:42.958Z","ordinal":16090,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a02f7e-eecd-73f1-9d58-3ef6316d2fff","author":"/root/phase2_quality_gate","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/phase2_quality_gate\nPayload:\nRead-only gate review complete. `go test ./internal/cli` and focused `-race` tests pass; `git diff --check` is clean.\n\nAssessment against `docs/candidate_distillation_plan.md`:\n\n- P2a (candidate packing/protocol): deterministic 232-member/30-pack accounting is internally consistent. Protocol parser is strict: expected IDs, missing/unknown IDs, blank/prose output, sentinel conflicts, per-member fact caps, taxonomy validation, and split retry are covered by tests.\n- P2b (cache/attribution/privacy): member cache identity is appropriately separated from packing, includes card/prompt/taxonomy/agent/model/effort/redaction, stores only canonical redacted results, and has relocation/append/no-op/corruption/privacy tests. Active Brain state remains untouched in shadow mode.\n- P2c (quality/performance evidence): not passable yet. The measured dry run proves deterministic filtering and projected call/byte reduction, not fact quality, provider token reduction, or latency.\n\nHIGH implementation/semantic gap:\n\n- Candidate admission only scans `user && DirectUser` turns (`internal/cli/distill_candidates.go:985-998`). Assistant-origin gotchas, discoveries, decisions, and closed negatives are never admitted—even with checkpoint, validation, recurrence, or later corroboration. The plan explicitly requires assistant claims to become eligible through those routes. This can prevent the ≥95% all-fact recall gate regardless of model quality.\n\nMEDIUM implementation gaps:\n\n- Split retries call the provider synchronously without acquiring the prefetch semaphore (`internal/cli/distill_shadow_v2.go:215-221`), so retries can exceed the configured concurrency cap while other prefetched packs remain in flight.\n- The shared authority prompt says “one … header” while v2 accepts multi-card packs; card-boundary/authority behavior has only fake-provider tests, not a real provider exercise.\n- The fixed 256 KiB provider output cap can reject a protocol-valid pack at the documented six-facts-per-member maximum (32 members × six × 2,000-byte facts), causing avoidable split/failure behavior. This needs output-budget handling, not pack-size tuning.\n- If a session has no `SessionID`, turn/candidate IDs fall back to transcript path (`distillCandidateSourceIdentityV1`), violating the documented relocation-stable identity contract.\n\nUncollected external evidence/blockers:\n\n- No human-labeled gold/span recall, 500-exchange filtered-out audit, injection rejection audit, or assistant-corroboration audit.\n- No paired legacy/candidate extraction with identical source cutoff, taxonomy/model/effort, repeated provider runs, or fact precision/recall/source-faithfulness measurements.\n- No proof that emitted facts are supported by their cited candidate span, nor retrieval-regression evaluation.\n- `1,415,420` candidate bytes are not provider input-token accounting: prompt/taxonomy bytes are repeated per call. The ≥85% token-reduction gate requires provider-reported usage or equivalent tokenization.\n- The 30 projected calls are deterministic uncached estimates, not observed provider calls; split retries, failures, and actual latency remain unmeasured. Also re-run the legacy comparison on the same 152 coalesced session views, since the 731/1,462 baseline used a different export set.\n\nConclusion: protocol/cache/privacy implementation is reasonably strong and tested, but Phase 2 cannot clear the plan’s exit gate. The assistant-candidate omission is the main implementation blocker; quality/recall/token/latency conclusions remain blocked on external human/model evaluation."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a02f65-7c17-7a30-9a2a-f255f8bc2ae4"}}}
