{"timestamp":"2026-08-23T16:51:04.637Z","ordinal":16435,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0873a68aa02aff8f016a8b24ece62081989c17497fda82951f","status":"completed","call_id":"call_jKXEVpoIp4wiHwunJFGbdz3N","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Add File: /Users/thomi/Projects/entire-brain/templates/entire-brain-distill-candidate-v2.md\\n+---\\n+name: entire-brain-distill-candidate-v2\\n+description: Distill packed candidate cards into candidate-ID-framed durable repository facts.\\n+---\\n+\\n+You are an expert note-taker for software-development work. You receive one or\\n+more compact candidate cards selected from conversations between a human and an\\n+AI coding agent. Judge every card independently and extract only durable facts\\n+that will help a future session rebuild important repository context.\\n+\\n+For each candidate, the default completion is NO_FACTS. Emit facts only when\\n+the evidence supports all four checks:\\n+\\n+1. DURABLE — still relevant a week or a month from now.\\n+2. USEFUL — genuinely helps a future session and is not obvious.\\n+3. NOT ALREADY KNOWN — not merely restating code, git, README, or seed context.\\n+4. WORTH WRITING DOWN — a senior engineer would keep it as onboarding memory.\\n+\\n+Good candidates include standing workflow rules, durable preferences, resolved\\n+choices with rationale, hard invariants, non-obvious gotchas, and closed\\n+negative results that say what failed, why, and when to revisit. Reject routine\\n+Q&A, one-off task instructions, implementation status, tool mechanics, plans,\\n+unresolved discussion, obvious code facts, and generic acknowledgements.\\n+\\n+Each fact has exactly one kind:\\n+\\n+- decision — a resolved choice and its rationale;\\n+- invariant — a must-hold constraint;\\n+- gotcha — a non-obvious trap or surprising behavior;\\n+- preference — how the human prefers work to be done;\\n+- convention — a standing process or style rule;\\n+- closed-negative — a rejected or failed path, its evidence, and revisit condition.\\n+\\n+Each fact must be one complete, self-contained statement. A closed-negative\\n+must include the attempted approach, why it failed or was rejected, and the\\n+condition for reconsidering it. Use only a valid three-level taxonomy path.\\n+\\n+${TAXONOMY_BLOCK}\\n+\\n+The candidate-card authority contract and exact output protocol follow. They\\n+are mandatory. Do not use an unframed legacy output format.\\n*** Update File: /Users/thomi/Projects/entire-brain/internal/cli/distill.go\\n@@\\n \\tdistillTemplateName              = \\\"templates/entire-brain-distill.md\\\"\\n+\\tdistillCandidateTemplateNameV2   = \\\"templates/entire-brain-distill-candidate-v2.md\\\"\\n@@\\n func renderDistillPromptForCandidateProtocolV2(taxonomy factTaxonomy) (string, error) {\\n-\\tprompt, err := renderDistillPrompt(taxonomy)\\n+\\tdata, err := entirebrain.Templates.ReadFile(distillCandidateTemplateNameV2)\\n \\tif err != nil {\\n-\\t\\treturn \\\"\\\", err\\n+\\t\\treturn \\\"\\\", fmt.Errorf(\\\"read candidate distill template: %w\\\", err)\\n \\t}\\n+\\tprompt := stripTemplateFrontmatter(string(data))\\n+\\tif !strings.Contains(prompt, distillTaxonomyMarker) {\\n+\\t\\treturn \\\"\\\", fmt.Errorf(\\\"candidate distill template missing %s marker\\\", distillTaxonomyMarker)\\n+\\t}\\n+\\tprompt = strings.ReplaceAll(prompt, distillTaxonomyMarker, factTaxonomyBlock(taxonomy))\\n \\treturn prompt + candidateDistillPromptAuthorityExtension + candidateDistillPromptProtocolV2, nil\\n }\\n*** Update File: /Users/thomi/Projects/entire-brain/internal/cli/distill_test.go\\n@@\\n \\tif strings.Contains(prompt, \\\"Candidate output must be either valid tab-separated fact lines\\\") {\\n \\t\\tt.Fatal(\\\"v2 candidate prompt retained the v1 output contract\\\")\\n \\t}\\n+\\tfor _, legacyConflict := range []string{\\n+\\t\\t\\\"Your default answer is NOTHING\\\",\\n+\\t\\t\\\"Each line is exactly: kind<TAB>path<TAB>fact\\\",\\n+\\t\\t\\\"Output 0–6 lines\\\",\\n+\\t} {\\n+\\t\\tif strings.Contains(prompt, legacyConflict) {\\n+\\t\\t\\tt.Fatalf(\\\"v2 candidate prompt retained conflicting legacy instruction %q\\\", legacyConflict)\\n+\\t\\t}\\n+\\t}\\n }\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a02f65-7c17-7a30-9a2a-f255f8bc2ae4"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-23T16:51:04.662Z","ordinal":16436,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a0200a-63d8-7b21-adef-c3850aecebf7","turn_id":"01a02f65-7c17-7a30-9a2a-f255f8bc2ae4","item":{"type":"FileChange","id":"exec-1fb8ba1f-8f4f-48ad-91ba-d34215a6ede4","changes":{"/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-brain/internal/cli/distill.go":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -14,2 +14,3 @@\n \tdistillTemplateName              = \"templates/entire-brain-distill.md\"\n+\tdistillCandidateTemplateNameV2   = \"templates/entire-brain-distill-candidate-v2.md\"\n \tdistillTaxonomyMarker            = \"${TAXONOMY_BLOCK}\"\n@@ -138,6 +139,11 @@\n func renderDistillPromptForCandidateProtocolV2(taxonomy factTaxonomy) (string, error) {\n-\tprompt, err := renderDistillPrompt(taxonomy)\n+\tdata, err := entirebrain.Templates.ReadFile(distillCandidateTemplateNameV2)\n \tif err != nil {\n-\t\treturn \"\", err\n+\t\treturn \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"read candidate distill template: %w\", err)\n+\t}\n+\tprompt := stripTemplateFrontmatter(string(data))\n+\tif !strings.Contains(prompt, distillTaxonomyMarker) {\n+\t\treturn \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"candidate distill template missing %s marker\", distillTaxonomyMarker)\n \t}\n+\tprompt = strings.ReplaceAll(prompt, distillTaxonomyMarker, factTaxonomyBlock(taxonomy))\n \treturn prompt + candidateDistillPromptAuthorityExtension + candidateDistillPromptProtocolV2, nil\n","move_path":null},"/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-brain/internal/cli/distill_test.go":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -74,2 +74,11 @@\n \t}\n+\tfor _, legacyConflict := range []string{\n+\t\t\"Your default answer is NOTHING\",\n+\t\t\"Each line is exactly: kind<TAB>path<TAB>fact\",\n+\t\t\"Output 0–6 lines\",\n+\t} {\n+\t\tif strings.Contains(prompt, legacyConflict) {\n+\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"v2 candidate prompt retained conflicting legacy instruction %q\", legacyConflict)\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n }\n","move_path":null},"/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-brain/templates/entire-brain-distill-candidate-v2.md":{"type":"add","content":"---\nname: entire-brain-distill-candidate-v2\ndescription: Distill packed candidate cards into candidate-ID-framed durable repository facts.\n---\n\nYou are an expert note-taker for software-development work. You receive one or\nmore compact candidate cards selected from conversations between a human and an\nAI coding agent. Judge every card independently and extract only durable facts\nthat will help a future session rebuild important repository context.\n\nFor each candidate, the default completion is NO_FACTS. Emit facts only when\nthe evidence supports all four checks:\n\n1. DURABLE — still relevant a week or a month from now.\n2. USEFUL — genuinely helps a future session and is not obvious.\n3. NOT ALREADY KNOWN — not merely restating code, git, README, or seed context.\n4. WORTH WRITING DOWN — a senior engineer would keep it as onboarding memory.\n\nGood candidates include standing workflow rules, durable preferences, resolved\nchoices with rationale, hard invariants, non-obvious gotchas, and closed\nnegative results that say what failed, why, and when to revisit. Reject routine\nQ&A, one-off task instructions, implementation status, tool mechanics, plans,\nunresolved discussion, obvious code facts, and generic acknowledgements.\n\nEach fact has exactly one kind:\n\n- decision — a resolved choice and its rationale;\n- invariant — a must-hold constraint;\n- gotcha — a non-obvious trap or surprising behavior;\n- preference — how the human prefers work to be done;\n- convention — a standing process or style rule;\n- closed-negative — a rejected or failed path, its evidence, and revisit condition.\n\nEach fact must be one complete, self-contained statement. A closed-negative\nmust include the attempted approach, why it failed or was rejected, and the\ncondition for reconsidering it. Use only a valid three-level taxonomy path.\n\n${TAXONOMY_BLOCK}\n\nThe candidate-card authority contract and exact output protocol follow. They\nare mandatory. Do not use an unframed legacy output format.\n"}},"status":"completed","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA /Users/thomi/Projects/entire-brain/templates/entire-brain-distill-candidate-v2.md\nM /Users/thomi/Projects/entire-brain/internal/cli/distill.go\nM /Users/thomi/Projects/entire-brain/internal/cli/distill_test.go\n","stderr":""},"started_at_ms":1787503864660,"completed_at_ms":1787503864662}}
