{"timestamp":"2026-08-23T16:54:03.297Z","ordinal":16521,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a0200a-63d8-7b21-adef-c3850aecebf7","turn_id":"01a02f65-7c17-7a30-9a2a-f255f8bc2ae4","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-17d1cfd4-73ae-4ce3-afbc-122bd6345204","process_id":"72139","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","transcript='/Users/thomi/.local/share/entire/plugins/data/brain/repos/gh/entireio/entire-graph/sessions/branches/docs-chicago-style-79b9eb59/20260821T045346Z_claude-code_22bc80ae-fe17-43c4-b918-a92250191246_8758c15f61fd.jsonl'; rg -n -i 'race test|Chicago style|Chicago' \"$transcript\" | head -30"],"cwd":"file:///Users/thomi/Projects/entire-brain","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"transcript='/Users/thomi/.local/share/entire/plugins/data/brain/repos/gh/entireio/entire-graph/sessions/branches/docs-chicago-style-79b9eb59/20260821T045346Z_claude-code_22bc80ae-fe17-43c4-b918-a92250191246_8758c15f61fd.jsonl'; rg -n -i 'race test|Chicago style|Chicago' \"$transcript\" | head -30"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"110:{\"parentUuid\":\"3ca0fec8-9e51-42dd-990b-ba5d8c42d94d\",\"isSidechain\":false,\"promptId\":\"9587fec6-f81e-4fec-a546-44b5af6770bc\",\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"make sure that the docs (and the Entire graph docs) are in Chicago style please\"},\"uuid\":\"69db7032-602a-42e8-a77e-1d84993f9dd7\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-21T02:58:44.292Z\",\"permissionMode\":\"bypassPermissions\",\"origin\":{\"kind\":\"human\"},\"promptSource\":\"typed\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/lizziesiegle/Desktop/entire-os/docs\",\"sessionId\":\"22bc80ae-fe17-43c4-b918-a92250191246\",\"version\":\"2.1.236\",\"gitBranch\":\"add-docs-for-graph\"}\n125:{\"type\":\"last-prompt\",\"lastPrompt\":\"make sure that the docs (and the Entire graph docs) are in Chicago style please\",\"leafUuid\":\"52e6761c-e1cb-460e-89ac-995ada04c32d\",\"sessionId\":\"22bc80ae-fe17-43c4-b918-a92250191246\"}\n131:{\"parentUuid\":\"6b1dacfd-8d79-482a-8a7b-eb426a13703c\",\"isSidechain\":false,\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011CeF9RCoDQ1JFQYF1rUTtG\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_01NJN3h514HTxSDWKomCCssd\",\"name\":\"AskUserQuestion\",\"input\":{\"questions\":[{\"question\":\"Chicago allows two heading conventions. Which one should I apply across every heading and frontmatter title?\",\"header\":\"Heading case\",\"multiSelect\":false,\"options\":[{\"label\":\"Headline style (CMOS 8.159)\",\"description\":\"Chicago's default for titles and headings. Capitalize first, last, and all major words; lowercase articles, coordinating conjunctions, and prepositions regardless of length. This is the bigger diff, since roughly half the docs are currently sentence case.\",\"preview\":\"## Set Up the Repo\\n## Where to Click First\\n## Choose a Voice\\n## Limits and Caveats\\n## Why Teams Turn It On\\n## Check That It Is Working\\n## Run entire-graph Directly\\n\\ntitle: Store Checkpoints in Another Repository\\ntitle: Security and Privacy\"},{\"label\":\"Sentence style (CMOS 8.158)\",\"description\":\"Chicago's sanctioned alternative, common in technical docs. Capitalize only the first word and proper nouns. Also a large diff, since the other half of the docs is currently title case.\",\"preview\":\"## Set up the repo\\n## Where to click first\\n## Choose a voice\\n## Limits and caveats\\n## Why teams turn it on\\n## Check that it is working\\n## Run entire-graph directly\\n\\ntitle: Store checkpoints in another repository\\ntitle: Security and privacy\"},{\"label\":\"Headline for titles, sentence for subheads\",\"description\":\"Frontmatter titles and H1-level page names in headline style, H2 and below in sentence style. Chicago permits this split for subordinate heads, and it is the smallest diff of the three.\",\"preview\":\"title: Store Checkpoints in Another Repository\\n\\n## Where to click first\\n## Limits and caveats\\n### Push through the mirror\"}]},{\"question\":\"Which trees should the Chicago pass cover? (docs/ and entire-graph/ are separate git repos.)\",\"header\":\"Scope\",\"multiSelect\":true,\"options\":[{\"label\":\"Public docs site (126 .mdx)\",\"description\":\"Everything in docs/ except the Mintlify boilerplate (essentials/) and the placeholder Plant API pages (api-reference/endpoint/), which are vendor template leftovers. Includes guides/graph/, the graph section of the public site.\"},{\"label\":\"entire-graph current docs (11 .md)\",\"description\":\"The top-level files in entire-graph/docs/: README, agents, commands, search, benchmarks, language-support, operations, snapshot-format, trust-and-security, semantic-provider-requirements, brain-and-graph-boundaries.\"},{\"label\":\"entire-graph archive, ADRs, evidence (16 .md)\",\"description\":\"Historical records: docs/archive/ dated plans, docs/adr/ decision records, docs/evidence/. Copyediting these rewrites the historical record, so I would skip them by default.\"},{\"label\":\"Mintlify boilerplate too\",\"description\":\"Also Chicago-ize essentials/ and the Plant API placeholder pages in api-reference/, which are unmodified Mintlify template files.\"}]}]},\"caller\":{\"type\":\"direct\"}}],\"stop_reason\":\"tool_use\",\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":1680,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":96170,\"output_tokens\":1339,\"output_tokens_details\":{\"thinking_tokens\":231},\"server_tool_use\":{\"web_search_requests\":0,\"web_fetch_requests\":0},\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":1680,\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0},\"inference_geo\":\"not_available\",\"iterations\":[{\"input_tokens\":2,\"output_tokens\":1339,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":96170,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":1680,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":1680},\"type\":\"message\"}],\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"diagnostics\":null},\"requestId\":\"req_011CeF9RBfWFjT3txDFeV72s\",\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"4471f028-d818-4287-a4e8-56ae30d67853\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-21T02:59:57.292Z\",\"effort\":\"high\",\"session_id\":\"286bdfa8-11e7-4200-9658-cb6d4ad68b10\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/lizziesiegle/Desktop/entire-os/docs\",\"sessionId\":\"22bc80ae-fe17-43c4-b918-a92250191246\",\"version\":\"2.1.236\",\"gitBranch\":\"add-docs-for-graph\"}\n132:{\"parentUuid\":\"4471f028-d818-4287-a4e8-56ae30d67853\",\"isSidechain\":false,\"promptId\":\"9587fec6-f81e-4fec-a546-44b5af6770bc\",\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"Your questions have been answered: \\\"Chicago allows two heading conventions. Which one should I apply across every heading and frontmatter title?\\\"=\\\"Headline for titles, sentence for subheads\\\" selected preview:\\ntitle: Store Checkpoints in Another Repository\\n\\n## Where to click first\\n## Limits and caveats\\n### Push through the mirror, \\\"Which trees should the Chicago pass cover? (docs/ and entire-graph/ are separate git repos.)\\\"=\\\"\\\"entire-graph archive, ADRs, evidence (16 .md)\\\", entire-graph current docs (11 .md), Public docs site (126 .mdx)\\\". You can now continue with these answers in mind.\",\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01NJN3h514HTxSDWKomCCssd\"}]},\"uuid\":\"2a181fcf-a571-4596-a426-f8861b8bb07a\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-21T03:11:11.418Z\",\"toolUseResult\":{\"questions\":[{\"question\":\"Chicago allows two heading conventions. Which one should I apply across every heading and frontmatter title?\",\"header\":\"Heading case\",\"options\":[{\"label\":\"Headline style (CMOS 8.159)\",\"description\":\"Chicago's default for titles and headings. Capitalize first, last, and all major words; lowercase articles, coordinating conjunctions, and prepositions regardless of length. This is the bigger diff, since roughly half the docs are currently sentence case.\",\"preview\":\"## Set Up the Repo\\n## Where to Click First\\n## Choose a Voice\\n## Limits and Caveats\\n## Why Teams Turn It On\\n## Check That It Is Working\\n## Run entire-graph Directly\\n\\ntitle: Store Checkpoints in Another Repository\\ntitle: Security and Privacy\"},{\"label\":\"Sentence style (CMOS 8.158)\",\"description\":\"Chicago's sanctioned alternative, common in technical docs. Capitalize only the first word and proper nouns. Also a large diff, since the other half of the docs is currently title case.\",\"preview\":\"## Set up the repo\\n## Where to click first\\n## Choose a voice\\n## Limits and caveats\\n## Why teams turn it on\\n## Check that it is working\\n## Run entire-graph directly\\n\\ntitle: Store checkpoints in another repository\\ntitle: Security and privacy\"},{\"label\":\"Headline for titles, sentence for subheads\",\"description\":\"Frontmatter titles and H1-level page names in headline style, H2 and below in sentence style. Chicago permits this split for subordinate heads, and it is the smallest diff of the three.\",\"preview\":\"title: Store Checkpoints in Another Repository\\n\\n## Where to click first\\n## Limits and caveats\\n### Push through the mirror\"}],\"multiSelect\":false},{\"question\":\"Which trees should the Chicago pass cover? (docs/ and entire-graph/ are separate git repos.)\",\"header\":\"Scope\",\"options\":[{\"label\":\"Public docs site (126 .mdx)\",\"description\":\"Everything in docs/ except the Mintlify boilerplate (essentials/) and the placeholder Plant API pages (api-reference/endpoint/), which are vendor template leftovers. Includes guides/graph/, the graph section of the public site.\"},{\"label\":\"entire-graph current docs (11 .md)\",\"description\":\"The top-level files in entire-graph/docs/: README, agents, commands, search, benchmarks, language-support, operations, snapshot-format, trust-and-security, semantic-provider-requirements, brain-and-graph-boundaries.\"},{\"label\":\"entire-graph archive, ADRs, evidence (16 .md)\",\"description\":\"Historical records: docs/archive/ dated plans, docs/adr/ decision records, docs/evidence/. Copyediting these rewrites the historical record, so I would skip them by default.\"},{\"label\":\"Mintlify boilerplate too\",\"description\":\"Also Chicago-ize essentials/ and the Plant API placeholder pages in api-reference/, which are unmodified Mintlify template files.\"}],\"multiSelect\":true}],\"answers\":{\"Chicago allows two heading conventions. Which one should I apply across every heading and frontmatter title?\":\"Headline for titles, sentence for subheads\",\"Which trees should the Chicago pass cover? (docs/ and entire-graph/ are separate git repos.)\":\"\\\"entire-graph archive, ADRs, evidence (16 .md)\\\", entire-graph current docs (11 .md), Public docs site (126 .mdx)\"},\"annotations\":{\"Chicago allows two heading conventions. Which one should I apply across every heading and frontmatter title?\":{\"preview\":\"title: Store Checkpoints in Another Repository\\n\\n## Where to click first\\n## Limits and caveats\\n### Push through the mirror\"}}},\"sourceToolAssistantUUID\":\"4471f028-d818-4287-a4e8-56ae30d67853\",\"session_id\":\"286bdfa8-11e7-4200-9658-cb6d4ad68b10\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/lizziesiegle/Desktop/entire-os/docs\",\"sessionId\":\"22bc80ae-fe17-43c4-b918-a92250191246\",\"version\":\"2.1.236\",\"gitBranch\":\"add-docs-for-graph\"}\n135:{\"parentUuid\":\"233e877d-2257-4fcf-8f26-b2a29e75f995\",\"isSidechain\":false,\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011CeFAJGRfqFbgdexfuDkyN\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Decisions noted: headline style for titles, sentence style for subheads; three trees in scope (public docs, entire-graph current docs, and the archive/ADR/evidence files). Let me survey what a Chicago pass 