rrently title case.\",\"preview\":\"## Set up the repo\\n## Where to click first\\n## Choose a voice\\n## Limits and caveats\\n## Why teams turn it on\\n## Check that it is working\\n## Run entire-graph directly\\n\\ntitle: Store checkpoints in another repository\\ntitle: Security and privacy\"},{\"label\":\"Headline for titles, sentence for subheads\",\"description\":\"Frontmatter titles and H1-level page names in headline style, H2 and below in sentence style. Chicago permits this split for subordinate heads, and it is the smallest diff of the three.\",\"preview\":\"title: Store Checkpoints in Another Repository\\n\\n## Where to click first\\n## Limits and caveats\\n### Push through the mirror\"}],\"multiSelect\":false},{\"question\":\"Which trees should the Chicago pass cover? (docs/ and entire-graph/ are separate git repos.)\",\"header\":\"Scope\",\"options\":[{\"label\":\"Public docs site (126 .mdx)\",\"description\":\"Everything in docs/ except the Mintlify boilerplate (essentials/) and the placeholder Plant API pages (api-reference/endpoint/), which are vendor template leftovers. Includes guides/graph/, the graph section of the public site.\"},{\"label\":\"entire-graph current docs (11 .md)\",\"description\":\"The top-level files in entire-graph/docs/: README, agents, commands, search, benchmarks, language-support, operations, snapshot-format, trust-and-security, semantic-provider-requirements, brain-and-graph-boundaries.\"},{\"label\":\"entire-graph archive, ADRs, evidence (16 .md)\",\"description\":\"Historical records: docs/archive/ dated plans, docs/adr/ decision records, docs/evidence/. Copyediting these rewrites the historical record, so I would skip them by default.\"},{\"label\":\"Mintlify boilerplate too\",\"description\":\"Also Chicago-ize essentials/ and the Plant API placeholder pages in api-reference/, which are unmodified Mintlify template files.\"}],\"multiSelect\":true}],\"answers\":{\"Chicago allows two heading conventions. Which one should I