{"timestamp":"2026-08-23T17:00:45.588Z","ordinal":16738,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0873a68aa02aff8f016a8b27302a0c8198bb2f3e98d2043371","status":"completed","call_id":"call_mzrARsuCwU84Qt4YqxEJTJVX","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /Users/thomi/Projects/entire-brain/docs/candidate_distillation_plan.md\\n@@\\n-Status: initial opt-in implementation complete and verified (2026-08-23).\\n+Status: Phase 2 shadow implementation complete; full quality exit gate pending\\n+(2026-08-23).\\n@@\\n-Legacy remains the default. Per-candidate persistent extraction caching,\\n-cross-session packing, repository-evidence corroboration, and default rollout\\n-remain later phases; they require the evaluation and privacy gates below.\\n+Legacy remains the default.\\n+\\n+The Phase 2 branch adds candidate-id-framed multi-card output, deterministic\\n+cross-session packing under a fixed 32 KiB/32-member policy, a bounded\\n+success-only member cache, one-level failure bisection, provider usage\\n+accounting, and `--shadow` execution that leaves active facts, proposals,\\n+taxonomy, the legacy cache, and the manifest unchanged. Exclude/purge resets the\\n+derived member cache; privacy verification, atomic-temp cleanup, and publish\\n+bundle exclusion cover the new artifact. Assistant claims gain one deliberately\\n+narrow repository-evidence route: an allowlisted successful checkpoint outcome\\n+plus an exact full-path mention from that session's touched-file list. Review\\n+sessions, status-only claims, basename matches, and unverified checkpoints do\\n+not qualify.\\n@@\\n-The final real-corpus dry-run of this slice against `entire-graph` (2026-08-23)\\n+The final Phase 1 real-corpus dry-run against `entire-graph` (2026-08-23)\\n@@\\n-remains necessary before a 30-60-call claim.\\n+remained necessary before a 30-60-call claim.\\n+\\n+### Phase 2 evidence (2026-08-23)\\n+\\n+Using the fixed policy without corpus-specific tuning, the current\\n+`entire-graph` shadow dry run reports 152 current session views, 367 admitted\\n+cards, 231 unique members after replay collapse, and 29 packs. Candidate input\\n+is 1,417,956 bytes versus 33,663,145 legacy-preprocessed bytes (95.8 percent\\n+less). The uncached extraction projection is 29 calls versus 731 legacy\\n+extraction calls (96.0 percent less), or 29 versus the 1,462 legacy\\n+extraction-plus-reconciliation ceiling (98.0 percent less). One cached member\\n+currently leaves the scheduled count at 29 because the remaining members still\\n+fill the same number of byte-bounded packs.\\n+\\n+The retained command for that projection is:\\n+\\n+```text\\n+entire-brain distill --dry-run --pipeline candidates --shadow \\\\\\n+  --agent ollama --model entire-brain-distill:qwen2.5-7b \\\\\\n+  /Users/thomi/Projects/entire-graph\\n+```\\n+\\n+A real local-model smoke on branch `docs/chicago-style` exposed two issues that\\n+fake-provider tests did not: the legacy output instructions conflicted with the\\n+framed protocol, and the model appended a redundant `NO_FACTS` after a valid\\n+fact. Phase 2 now uses a dedicated non-conflicting prompt and accepts only that\\n+content-free trailing sentinel form (a leading sentinel followed by facts still\\n+fails closed). The final run admitted one source-backed Chicago-style rule,\\n+completed one packed call in 10.66 seconds, reported 2,497 input and 150 output\\n+tokens, and produced one faithful shadow fact. The immediate rerun was a\\n+zero-call member-cache hit in 37 milliseconds. A task-local “do not change any\\n+files or code” request found during the same audit is now deterministically\\n+suppressed rather than promoted as a standing rule.\\n+\\n+This passes the implementation, isolation, fixed-policy call-count, and small\\n+real-provider protocol checks. It does **not** pass Phase 2's full exit gate:\\n+one manually inspected fact is not a labeled corpus. Promotion beyond shadow\\n+still requires the human-labeled span recall/precision audit, filtered-out\\n+negative sample, repeated paired legacy/candidate provider runs, source-anchor\\n+faithfulness review, and observed provider token/latency totals described below.\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a02f65-7c17-7a30-9a2a-f255f8bc2ae4"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-23T17:00:45.608Z","ordinal":16739,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a0200a-63d8-7b21-adef-c3850aecebf7","turn_id":"01a02f65-7c17-7a30-9a2a-f255f8bc2ae4","item":{"type":"FileChange","id":"exec-c0eecab9-3a37-4739-af32-bc0fab6a39f3","changes":{"/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-brain/docs/candidate_distillation_plan.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -2,3 +2,4 @@\n \n-Status: initial opt-in implementation complete and verified (2026-08-23).\n+Status: Phase 2 shadow implementation complete; full quality exit gate pending\n+(2026-08-23).\n \n@@ -9,6 +10,16 @@\n keys, dry-run accounting, redaction, and privacy-linearized egress/publication.\n-Legacy remains the default. Per-candidate persistent extraction caching,\n-cross-session packing, repository-evidence corroboration, and default rollout\n-remain later phases; they require the evaluation and privacy gates below.\n+Legacy remains the default.\n \n+The Phase 2 branch adds candidate-id-framed multi-card output, deterministic\n+cross-session packing under a fixed 32 KiB/32-member policy, a bounded\n+success-only member cache, one-level failure bisection, provider usage\n+accounting, and `--shadow` execution that leaves active facts, proposals,\n+taxonomy, the legacy cache, and the manifest unchanged. Exclude/purge resets the\n+derived member cache; privacy verification, atomic-temp cleanup, and publish\n+bundle exclusion cover the new artifact. Assistant claims gain one deliberately\n+narrow repository-evidence route: an allowlisted successful checkpoint outcome\n+plus an exact full-path mention from that session's touched-file list. Review\n+sessions, status-only claims, basename matches, and unverified checkpoints do\n+not qualify.\n+\n The opt-in slice keeps each complete redacted authoritative trigger turn. It\n@@ -20,3 +31,3 @@\n \n-The final real-corpus dry-run of this slice against `entire-graph` (2026-08-23)\n+The final Phase 1 real-corpus dry-run against `entire-graph` (2026-08-23)\n completed without an unsupported-dialect fallback. The legacy path sees 154\n@@ -30,3 +41,42 @@\n filtering works, not that the latency goal is met: candidate-id-framed packing\n-remains necessary before a 30-60-call claim.\n+remained necessary before a 30-60-call claim.\n+\n+### Phase 2 evidence (2026-08-23)\n+\n+Using the fixed policy without corpus-specific tuning, the current\n+`entire-graph` shadow dry run reports 152 current session views, 367 admitted\n+cards, 231 unique members after replay collapse, and 29 packs. Candidate input\n+is 1,417,956 bytes versus 33,663,145 legacy-preprocessed bytes (95.8 percent\n+less). The uncached extraction projection is 29 calls versus 731 legacy\n+extraction calls (96.0 percent less), or 29 versus the 1,462 legacy\n+extraction-plus-reconciliation ceiling (98.0 percent less). One cached member\n+currently leaves the scheduled count at 29 because the remaining members still\n+fill the same number of byte-bounded packs.\n+\n+The retained command for that projection is:\n+\n+```text\n+entire-brain distill --dry-run --pipeline candidates --shadow \\\n+  --agent ollama --model entire-brain-distill:qwen2.5-7b \\\n+  /Users/thomi/Projects/entire-graph\n+```\n+\n+A real local-model smoke on branch `docs/chicago-style` exposed two issues that\n+fake-provider tests did not: the legacy output instructions conflicted with the\n+framed protocol, and the model appended a redundant `NO_FACTS` after a valid\n+fact. Phase 2 now uses a dedicated non-conflicting prompt and accepts only that\n+content-free trailing sentinel form (a leading sentinel followed by facts still\n+fails closed). The final run admitted one source-backed Chicago-style rule,\n+completed one packed call in 10.66 seconds, reported 2,497 input and 150 output\n+tokens, and produced one faithful shadow fact. The immediate rerun was a\n+zero-call member-cache hit in 37 milliseconds. A task-local “do not change any\n+files or code” request found during the same audit is now deterministically\n+suppressed rather than promoted as a standing rule.\n+\n+This passes the implementation, isolation, fixed-policy call-count, and small\n+real-provider protocol checks. It does **not** pass Phase 2's full exit gate:\n+one manually inspected fact is not a labeled corpus. Promotion beyond shadow\n+still requires the human-labeled span recall/precision audit, filtered-out\n+negative sample, repeated paired legacy/candidate provider runs, source-anchor\n+faithfulness review, and observed provider token/latency totals described below.\n \n","move_path":null}},"status":"completed","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM /Users/thomi/Projects/entire-brain/docs/candidate_distillation_plan.md\n","stderr":""},"started_at_ms":1787504445608,"completed_at_ms":1787504445608}}
