{"timestamp":"2026-08-23T17:03:06.250Z","ordinal":16796,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a02f93-6e0a-7cb0-a497-1a468b10860d","author":"/root/phase2_quality_gate","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/phase2_quality_gate\nPayload:\nLatest review: the new slice is substantially better. `go test ./internal/cli`, focused `-race` tests, `go vet ./internal/cli`, and `git diff --check` pass.\n\nGate arithmetic is favorable:\n\n- 1.418 MB candidate bytes vs 33.663 MB legacy preprocessing: ~95.8% reduction.\n- 29 projected extraction packs vs 731 legacy extraction calls: ~96.0% fewer.\n- 29 vs 1,462 extraction+reconcile upper bound: ~98.0% fewer.\n- Chicago smoke demonstrates one real provider call, 2,497 input/150 output tokens, source-faithful output, and a zero-call 37 ms rerun.\n\nBlocker-level code findings:\n\n1. V2 parser does not actually restrict redundant `NO_FACTS` to trailing position (`internal/cli/distill_protocol_v2.go:87-103`).\n\n   This malformed sequence is accepted:\n\n   ```text\n   candidate<TAB>fact...\n   candidate<TAB>NO_FACTS\n   candidate<TAB>another fact...\n   ```\n\n   The sentinel is ignored once facts exist, and later facts remain accepted. The existing test covers only leading-sentinel rejection and a final redundant sentinel. Either require a redundant sentinel to be the final nonblank output line, or at minimum reject any later fact for that candidate after the sentinel. Until fixed, malformed model output can be cached as protocol-valid.\n\n2. Assistant “status-only” suppression is prefix-based rather than status-only (`internal/cli/distill_candidates.go:1027-1031`).\n\n   Any assistant turn beginning with `Implemented`, `Fixed`, `Completed`, `Shipped`, or `Tests passed` is rejected even when it continues with durable rationale or a gotcha, e.g.:\n\n   ```text\n   Fixed internal/cache.go: the stale descriptor survives because ...\n   ```\n\n   The plan calls generic implementation status a negative signal, not a hard rejection. This can materially reduce assistant-origin recall. Narrow the regex to complete status-only statements, or evaluate cues first and suppress only when no durable content follows.\n\nNon-blocking implementation concern:\n\n- The checkpoint corroboration is intentionally conservative, but `FilesTouched` and `Summary.Outcome` are session/checkpoint metadata rather than turn-level proof. The exact-file requirement prevents treating every checkpoint as evidence, but it remains a heuristic corroboration route and needs labeled validation.\n\nExternal Phase-2 evidence still missing:\n\n- No full-corpus labeled candidate span recall (98% explicit rules/negatives, 95% all durable facts).\n- No 500-item filtered-out audit.\n- No paired legacy/candidate extraction on the same source cutoff with human fact labels, repeated provider runs, source-faithfulness/anchor scoring, authority/corroboration scoring, or retrieval comparison.\n- The 2,497-token Chicago smoke is useful plumbing evidence only; it cannot establish corpus token reduction or latency.\n- Byte reduction is not provider-token reduction because prompt/taxonomy tokens repeat per pack.\n- No evidence yet for interruption loss, split-retry frequency, or real-provider protocol-invalid rates.\n\nHonest gate assessment: deterministic packing, prompt isolation, cache/privacy behavior, and the projected operational reductions are now credible. Phase 2 still does not clear its quality exit gate until the two parser/status issues are addressed and the labeled paired evaluation is collected."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a02f65-7c17-7a30-9a2a-f255f8bc2ae4"}}}
