{"timestamp":"2026-08-23T17:45:28.312Z","ordinal":17124,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a02fba-37f8-7c80-96f5-68eeb00fc1ea","author":"/root/phase3_integration_map","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/phase3_integration_map\nPayload:\nRead-only integration map (worktree clean).\n\nThe smallest safe Phase 3A is a new v2 apply path, not an extension of the existing live candidate loop. Current live `--pipeline candidates` is Phase 1: one card/call, v1 prompt/parser, session-fingerprint cache, and anchor-removal cleanup. Phase 2’s authoritative artifacts are framed-member results in `facts/distill-candidate-results-v2.ndjson`, but its runner is explicitly shadow-only.\n\n**Exact handoff**\n\n- Entry: `runDistillForBrain` in `internal/cli/distill_cmd.go`.\n  - It already does privacy locking, tombstone filtering, same-branch re-export coalescing, deterministic session sort, complete candidate preflight snapshots, and branch resolution.\n  - Its `if distillOpts.shadow { return runDistillCandidateShadowV2(...) }` at ~950 is the correct seam to branch toward `runDistillCandidateApplyV2(...)` for non-shadow candidate execution.\n- V2 source/material:\n  - Cards/anchors: `preparedDistillSessionInput.CandidateBatches`, `distillCandidateAnchorV1` in `distill_candidates.go`.\n  - Pack types: `distillCandidatePackMemberV2` / `distillCandidatePackV2` in `distill_packing_v2.go`.\n  - Protocol: `parseDistillCandidateMemberResultsV2` in `distill_protocol_v2.go`.\n  - Canonical cached facts: `distillCandidateCacheResultV2` / `distillCandidateCachedFactV2`, validated by `canonicalDistillCandidateCacheResultV2` in `distill_shadow_v2.go`.\n  - Provider execution, bisection, capped cache persistence, usage: `runDistillCandidateShadowV2`, `runDistillCandidatePackAttemptV2`, and `startDistillCandidatePackPrefetchV2`.\n- Materialization:\n  - Construct ordinary `factRecord`s from cached v2 facts, assigning `ID: factRecordID(text, paths)`, target branch, distilled/active origin/status, locus, timestamps, and an anchor built from the card anchor.\n  - Apply only `newDistilledFactActions(records)` then `applyFactActions(...)`; `factmerge.Upsert` performs exact-ID provenance union. This is already the desired exact-only behavior.\n  - Persist via the existing locked/digest-checked machinery: `loadFacts`, `writeFacts`, `loadFactProposals`, `writeFactProposals`, and `updateBrainManifestAndReadme`.\n\n**Do not reuse the Phase 1 writer as-is**\n\nThe current non-shadow candidate loop at `distill_cmd.go:1211–1344` invokes `distilledFactsFromOutput` and `candidateDistillOutputIsProtocolComplete`, which accept the old unframed grammar. It also calls `removeRelocatedDistillAnchors` and `removeMissingDistillTurnAnchors` keyed by `(sessionID, DistillTurnID)`. That is incompatible with a packed response: it has neither member-level cache reuse nor a durable “which v2 result was applied to which branch/provenance” record.\n\nA Phase 3A apply helper should consume the v2 cache first, fetch/cache only misses using the existing Phase 2 pack runner, then apply member results in canonical source order. Keep a per-candidate list of application targets; Phase 2’s `byCandidate` intentionally collapses duplicate member views for extraction and currently retains only one `SourceSessionID`, insufficient for all branch/provenance materializations.\n\n**Branch/provenance semantics**\n\n- Candidate IDs are source-content identities: `selectDistillCandidateCardsV1` derives them from source session identity and turn IDs, deliberately excluding checkpoint/path. Extraction can therefore be reused across re-export/checkpoint/branch views.\n- Materialization must remain branch-scoped. For each branch view, create/union an anchor using the branch’s `distillCandidateAnchorV1`.\n- Reuse `factAnchor.DistillTurnID` for candidate ownership only if populated with the stable candidate ID (or add an explicit candidate ID to the receipt). Do not key cleanup only on the physical line range: re-exports may move it.\n- Exact same fact ID across legacy and v2 must union anchors and retain the legacy anchor. Existing `factmerge.Upsert`/`UnionAnchors` already do this.\n- No automatic paraphrase, merge, or supersession. `newDistilledFactActions` is exactly correct for this slice.\n\n**Different-ID proposals**\n\nDefer them in 3A unless the implementation can name a specific `merge` or `supersede` action and target without heuristic taxonomy-path matching. The existing queue (`factProposal`) only models concrete `(action, candidate fact ID, target fact ID)` and review will execute that action; it cannot represent “possibly related” safely. Creating `merge` proposals for all path-neighbors would turn vague similarity into an executable recommendation. Thus: add distinct facts, no proposals, and document the explicit deferral. This is safer than the plan’s eventual “queue all different-id relationships” language.\n\n**Force vs incremental**\n\n- Incremental v2 must be additive: load current branch facts and only exact-upsert v2 records; never call the Phase 1 anchor-deletion helpers unless a v2 receipt proves this exact candidate/provenance was previously applied. This preserves legacy-distilled and authored facts.\n- Current generic force removes every `Origin == distilled` record in `ensureBranch` (~1000); candidate force therefore correctly rebuilds from candidate inputs but must not accidentally use a stale v1 session cache.\n- Preserve the existing force scope implementation, including orphan branch inventory and retention of member-attributed proposals:\n  `distillForceScopeBranches`, `flushFactStoresLocked`, `clearDistillOwnedLegacyProposalStore`.\n- `--session --force` remains forbidden, correctly.\n- Current force clears both legacy and candidate session-cache namespaces in scope. For 3A, it should also invalidate/rebuild **application receipts**, but should normally retain V2 extraction cache entries: force rebuilds materialization, not valid extraction work. The plan’s “all v2 stages” wording conflicts with its independent cache-layer goals; retaining content-addressed extraction results is the smaller, safer interpretation unless explicit force semantics require provider re-extraction.\n\n**Receipts are the missing required piece**\n\nNo application receipt store exists. The v2 cache stores result ownership only (`SourceSessionID`), not `(extraction identity/result, branch, provenance, fact-store generation)`. Add a bounded, atomic, privacy-inventoried `facts/distill-v2/applications.ndjson` (or equivalent) before live application.\n\nMinimum receipt fields:\n\n- candidate ID + extraction identity digest\n- branch\n- provenance identity digest (session/checkpoint/transcript/lines/candidate ID)\n- resulting fact IDs (including an explicit empty application)\n- fact-store generation/digest\n- enough source-session ownership for tombstone purge\n\nThis lets incremental runs skip only a proven identical application, replay changed provenance without provider work, and remove/reconcile only prior v2-owned anchors. It also avoids using the Phase 1 “remove all trigger-owned anchors before each result” behavior.\n\n**Manifest/status**\n\n- Current `factSourceManifest` already holds command-result candidate metrics, but `runDistillForBrain` explicitly zeroes all candidate-specific fields and `Pipeline` before schema-v3 manifest publication (~1416). This matches the plan: do not add candidate fields to the strict existing manifest in 3A.\n- Return v2 metrics in the command JSON and dry-run report. `facts status --json` already exposes `ManifestFacts`, but cannot report V2 cache/apply health.\n- If status is required in 3A, add a separately versioned status leaf/report rather than extending `manifest.json`; otherwise defer “current/stale/partially reusable/corrupt” until the receipt/state schema exists.\n\n**High-risk pitfalls**\n\n- **High:** Wiring non-shadow candidates through `startSessionPrefetch` yields old single-card/v1 outputs and bypasses the v2 result cache/atomic member protocol.\n- **High:** Applying `removeRelocatedDistillAnchors`/`removeMissingDistillTurnAnchors` without v2 receipts can retract v2-derived facts on a merely changed model/prompt or incomplete pack outcome.\n- **High:** Phase 2 deduplicates members for extraction; losing the duplicate application targets would silently omit branch provenance.\n- **High:** Empty results must receive receipts. A protocol-valid `NO_FACTS` cannot be treated as a failed/unapplied member, and a malformed/failed member must never clear prior application.\n- **High:** Register receipts in privacy purge/verify and publish exclusion. V2 cache is already covered in `session_privacy.go`, `session_privacy_verify.go`, and publish tests; a new application artifact must be added to the same inventories.\n- **Medium:** The existing v2 cache key is candidate ID → one entry. If candidate IDs collide across distinct source owners, `PutSuccess` overwrites. Shadow currently rejects inconsistent duplicate rendered views but materialization should retain all valid application views.\n- **Medium:** Existing `factProposal` lacks rationale/feature provenance, so premature relationship proposals are opaque and executable.\n- **Medium:** `factSourceManifest` summary currently computes fact count globally after writes; preserve this behavior for branch-scoped incremental runs.\n\n**Recommended sequence**\n\n1. Extract/refactor the Phase 2 member collection/cache/fetch flow into a reusable helper returning ordered member results plus every branch/provenance application target; keep shadow as a no-materialization caller.\n2. Add the versioned application-receipt store with strict parsing, atomic writes, tombstone/purge/verify/publish inventory, and receipt-level idempotency helpers.\n3. Implement pure v2 result → `factRecord` construction and exact-only application (`newDistilledFactActions` + `applyFactActions`), recording an empty receipt too.\n4. Add `runDistillCandidateApplyV2` under the existing privacy lock and existing lock/digest-checked fact/proposal flush conventions; leave legacy behavior untouched.\n5. Route only `--pipeline candidates` without `--shadow` to it; retain shadow unchanged.\n6. Reconcile force as a receipt reset plus current distilled-layer replacement, preserve authored/attributed proposals, and decide explicitly whether force reuses valid extraction cache.\n7. Surface v2 command/dry-run metrics; defer durable manifest/status fields until the independently versioned leaf is accepted.\n\n**Best existing test seams**\n\n- V2 parsing/atomicity: `distill_protocol_v2_test.go`.\n- Fixed packing/order/limits: `distill_packing_v2_test.go`.\n- Cache identity/corruption: `distill_cache_v2_test.go`.\n- End-to-end extraction/cache/bisection/isolation: `distill_shadow_v2_test.go`.\n- Existing live safety baselines: `distill_cmd_test.go` tests:\n  `TestCandidatePipelinePreservesLegacyRollbackCacheUnlessForced`,\n  `TestCandidateEmptyReprocessDoesNotDeleteLegacyOwnedFact`,\n  `TestCandidatePipelineSkipsModelReconciliation`,\n  `TestCandidatePipelineBlankPreservesAndSentinelClearsMaterialization`,\n  and concurrent fact-admin protection.\n- Exact union and legacy/candidate ownership: `internal/factmerge/factmerge_test.go` (`TestUnionAnchorsKeepsLegacyAndCandidateOwnershipDistinct`, `TestUpsertDedupesAndUnionsProvenance`).\n- Privacy and publishing coverage: `session_privacy*_test.go`, `session_privacy_verify.go`, and `publish_test.go`.\n\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a02fb8-5db4-77e3-a158-975075162964"}}}
