{"timestamp":"2026-08-23T17:51:38.768Z","ordinal":17280,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a02fbf-df10-7d82-93d2-89a13683ac50","call_id":"call_xEtt2r1uWlMa736se2LEUeW6","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/phase3_gate_design\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"Phase 3A should be an opt-in, exact-only write gate—not a default-rollout gate. The current branch passes focused CLI tests, but it is not yet promotable as the Phase 2 packed pipeline: `runDistillCandidateShadowV2` is shadow-only, while non-shadow candidate writes still consume the older one-card/session-cache path. Its V2 member cache has no write-materialization/application-receipt layer.\\n\\n## Required Phase 3A gates\\n\\n| Area | Measurable acceptance gate |\\n|---|---|\\n| Pipeline identity | Non-shadow `--pipeline candidates` must consume the same candidate-id-framed, cross-session packed member results as shadow. For a frozen fixture, dry-run, shadow, and write mode have identical admitted member IDs/order, cache hits/misses, packs, provider calls, parsed facts, and anchor mapping (apart from intentional writes). |\\n| Semantic admission | Gold labels: ≥98% span recall for direct human standing rules/preferences/revisions/closed negatives; ≥95% over all durable facts; 100% rejection of proven injected system/developer/tool/hook/skill text; no review-only claim becomes active. Audit ≥500 deterministically sampled filtered exchanges with zero critical miss. |\\n| Fact quality | Three paired legacy/candidate runs with identical cutoff/prompt/taxonomy/model/effort. Candidate recall is no worse than legacy by 2 percentage points; durable precision is at least legacy; 100% emitted facts have a cited supporting span and exact anchor. |\\n| Exact merge | For every same `factmerge.RecordID`, exactly one record remains; normalized text + sorted paths identity is correct 100%; provenance is the ordered union with no duplicate physical anchor; valid existing kind is not overwritten. Test same text/path across sessions, branches, relocation, and legacy/candidate ownership. |\\n| Different IDs | 3A performs no automatic paraphrase merge and no automatic supersession: counters must be zero. Any detected ambiguous relationship is a visible, deduplicated proposal; unrelated same-taxonomy-path facts must neither merge nor produce a misleading relationship. |\\n| Force/incremental parity | Starting from identical fixtures and fixed time, (a) clean forced candidate rebuild and (b) incremental candidate replay converge to byte-identical canonical facts/proposals after normalizing generated timestamps/run metadata. Cover branch/session filters, exact duplicate, relocation, changed checkpoint with unchanged content, cache corruption, and interrupted force. |\\n| Legacy preservation | Incremental candidate writes preserve authored facts and pre-existing legacy-distilled facts; exact candidate matches only union provenance. `--force --pipeline candidates` must show the exact affected branch/store scope before execution and retain authored plus member-attributed cross-member proposals. |\\n| Relocation/removal | Moving an unchanged transcript or replaying it on another branch makes zero extraction calls and only updates provenance/materialization. Replacing/removing a candidate removes only its own anchors; a fact with other anchors survives; explicit successful `NO_FACTS` removes prior materialization for that member, while blank/invalid output removes nothing. |\\n| Failure/interrupt | Failed/invalid pack members are never cached or materialized; one bisection level salvages successful neighbors; repeated total provider misconfiguration fails fast. Kill at every persistence boundary and resume: no duplicate facts/proposals, no missing successful member result, and loss is bounded by the documented completed-pack flush interval (currently 50 calls unless changed). |\\n| Privacy/publish | Tombstone/exclude precedes lookup and egress; purge removes/reset all v2-derived state plus anchors/derived indexes; malformed/opaque cache is a privacy failure but purge-safe. Verify 0600, symlink/path traversal, atomic-temp cleanup, no plaintext cards/log excerpts, no-egress dry run, and publish bundle exclusion. |\\n| Dry-run truthfulness | Dry-run must construct the exact immutable plan used by execution: real V2 member cache hits, packs/calls, candidate bytes, force deletion scope, and zero reconcile calls. Estimated tokens must remain explicitly estimates; it must make zero provider/network calls and write no state. |\\n| Performance | On the frozen `entire-graph` corpus with declared cache state, measure—not project—≥80% fewer extraction calls than 64 KiB legacy, ≥90% fewer total calls than legacy extraction+reconcile, ≥85% fewer provider input tokens, zero candidate reconcile calls, zero-call no-op/no-candidate append/relocation/branch replay/confidence change, and ≤1 pack for one isolated candidate append. Retain provider tokens and wall time for all three paired runs. |\\n\\nCurrent retained Phase 2 projection is strong but only a projection: 29 packs versus 731 legacy extraction calls (96% fewer) and 1.418 MB versus 33.663 MB input (95.8% fewer). It cannot support latency or quality claims until the paired real-provider corpus evidence exists.\\n\\n## Current code hazards / blockers\\n\\n1. **V2 cannot yet be promoted.** `internal/cli/distill_shadow_v2.go` explicitly permits only the member-result cache; normal writes in `distill_cmd.go` still use the Phase-1 `CandidateBatches`/session fingerprint route. Do not call this Phase 3A complete until V2 cache results are materialized through deterministic reconciliation and branch/provenance receipts.\\n\\n2. **No V2 application receipt/provenance model.** The current V2 cache owns only one `SourceSessionID`; it lacks branch-specific application identity and anchor data needed for branch replay, exact removal, and force/incremental convergence.\\n\\n3. **Different-ID proposal requirement is missing.** `newDistilledFactActions` makes every different ID a new fact. This is safely exact-only, but it does not queue any relationship proposal. Either implement a deliberately bounded proposal detector or narrow the 3A promise to “keep separate without proposing.”\\n\\n4. **Dry-run is shadow-specific for pack/cache accounting.** `buildDistillDryRunReportContext` consults V2 member cache/packs only under `--shadow`. Once V2 writes exist, non-shadow dry-run would otherwise misstate actual cache/call behavior.\\n\\n5. **Current “candidate” cache is a session fingerprint in write mode.** It cannot prove member-level no-op/append/repack behavior, despite the V2 shadow cache proving some of it.\\n\\n6. **Force parity must include failure windows.** Existing legacy-oriented force safeguards are substantial, but V2 write integration must protect unvisited facts and non-distill-owned proposals across mid-run flush/cancel.\\n\\n7. **Corpus-general input remains unresolved.** The plan records that cue-bearing pasted documents can exceed the card ceiling and require cue-span/paragraph splitting. Complete-or-refused is safe, but it blocks a corpus-general recall claim.\\n\\n8. **Exact identity is intentionally narrow.** Record IDs normalize only case/whitespace plus sorted paths. Punctuation/code-quote variants remain different IDs, correctly for 3A; do not silently treat them as “exact.”\\n\\nFocused regression tests currently pass:\\n\\n```text\\ngo test ./internal/cli -run 'TestCandidate(ShadowV2|Pipeline|Pack|DistillOutput)|TestPrivacyOwnsCandidateResultCacheV2|TestPublish' -count=1\\n```\\n\\n## Explicitly defer past 3A\\n\\n- Automatic paraphrase merge until a retained labeled-pair precision result is ≥99%.\\n- Any automatic different-ID supersession; keep it at zero until 100% supersession precision is demonstrated.\\n- Defaulting candidate mode, removing legacy, or marketing speed/quality/recall.\\n- Session-end/watch integration (Phase 4).\\n- Retrieval-win claims until paired proof-labeled facts-eval evidence.\\n- Hosted-provider latency claims and corpus-general recall claims until the large pasted-document issue and labeled corpus are covered.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/phase3_materializer\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"Implemented in new files only:\\n\\n- `internal/cli/distill_materialize_v2.go`\\n- `internal/cli/distill_materialize_v2_test.go`\\n\\nAPI:\\n\\n- `materializeDistillCandidateResultV2(result, target, now)`\\n- `applyDistillCandidateResultV2(active, result, target, now)`\\n\\nBehavior includes strict result/target validation, explicit empty success, deterministic content-derived IDs, sorted receipt-facing `FactIDs`, exact provenance anchors, distilled/active timestamps, authored/legacy anchor preservation, and exact-only application through `newDistilledFactActions`/`applyFactActions`.\\n\\nFocused tests pass:\\n\\n```text\\ngo test ./internal/cli -run 'Test(Materialize|ApplyDistillCandidate)' -count=1\\nok\\n```\\n\\nThe full CLI suite was started but interrupted after several minutes due unrelated long-running integration tests.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/phase3_receipts\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a02fb8-5db4-77e3-a158-975075162964"}}}
