{"timestamp":"2026-08-23T18:03:32.447Z","ordinal":17648,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a02fca-c2df-7be3-aa62-c4fa2e9bb3dd","author":"/root/phase3_quality_review","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/phase3_quality_review\nPayload:\nQuality review complete: no HIGH/MEDIUM blockers found in the reviewed Phase 3A scope.\n\nVerified:\n\n- v2 parser rejects unknown/missing/duplicate IDs and attributes facts by exact candidate ID.\n- Packing is deterministic and bounded to 32 KiB/32 members without rewriting cards.\n- Materialization is exact-only; different fact IDs remain separate and no proposals are generated.\n- Exact duplicates union provenance while preserving legacy/authored records.\n- Relocation updates only the candidate-owned anchor; corroborating/legacy anchors survive.\n- `NO_FACTS` retracts only that candidate’s v2-owned materialization.\n- Live, shadow, and dry-run paths use the same v2 prompt, snapshots, packing, and cache identity.\n- Focused candidate/protocol/materialization/application tests pass.\n\nThe formal quality gate remains pending: labeled span recall/precision, paired legacy-vs-candidate evaluation, filtered-out negative audit, and real provider token/latency evidence. The docs should also explicitly record that different-ID relationship proposals are deferred in Phase 3A."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a02fb8-5db4-77e3-a158-975075162964"}}}
