{"timestamp":"2026-08-23T18:08:59.683Z","ordinal":17849,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a02fcf-c123-71f2-ad33-237a50752ab6","call_id":"call_QElHiQYypKEEzpmEA9fSYPnT","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/phase3_perf_review\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"Audit complete; sent measured parity, test evidence, and remaining Phase 3 gates to the parent. No high performance/parity blocker found.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/phase3_quality_review\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"Re-review findings:\\n\\n- Exact/no-op/relocation semantics still pass the focused candidate tests.\\n- Slot-wide cleanup is correctly bounded by `SessionID + CandidateID`; it cannot affect another generated candidate/session because generated v2 candidate IDs are content-addressed with the source session identity.\\n- Phase 1 generated anchors use `turn-v1:` IDs, while v2 uses `candidate-v1:`, so normal Phase 1 anchors are outside the cleanup namespace.\\n- Receipt-specific cleanup preserves exact legacy-backed facts and corroborating anchors.\\n\\nOne MEDIUM hardening concern remains: the crash-recovery/force sweep identifies v2 ownership solely by the `candidate-v1:` prefix and does not check `Origin`. A manually authored or legacy record containing a provenance anchor with that prefix could have that anchor stripped; a distilled record with only such an anchor could be removed. Generated legacy records appear to use `turn-v1:` or empty IDs, so this is not an observed-path failure, but it means the “cannot delete authored/legacy” invariant is not absolute for arbitrary persisted anchors. A stronger ownership marker or an explicit `Origin`/receipt guard would close it.\\n\\nNo other HIGH/MEDIUM issues found.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/phase3_runtime_review\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"One medium scope regression found: unscoped force/dry-run now includes every fact branch, including legacy-only orphan branches. The existing focused test fails on that scope expansion. Limit discovery to branches with v2 anchors or v2 receipts so crash recovery remains complete without claiming unrelated stores.\"}}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a02fb8-5db4-77e3-a158-975075162964"}}}
