{"timestamp":"2026-08-23T18:09:43.824Z","ordinal":17874,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a02fd0-6d90-7bd2-b1ab-d5b2f4b4cfb6","author":"/root/phase3_quality_review","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/phase3_quality_review\nPayload:\nFinal ownership review: no HIGH/MEDIUM blockers found.\n\n- v2 materialization now writes `candidate-application-v2:<64hex>` anchors, derived only from validated `candidate-v1:<64hex>` IDs.\n- Cleanup validates that marker before deriving candidate ownership.\n- Receipt cleanup uses the same marker and still scopes by recorded fact ID plus source session.\n- Phase 1 `turn-v1:` anchors, ordinary legacy anchors, and unrelated candidate/session anchors remain outside the cleanup namespace.\n- Force and incremental cleanup preserve corroborating anchors; exact/no-op, relocation, `NO_FACTS`, and crash-retry semantics remain intact.\n- Focused tests pass:\n\n```text\ngo test ./internal/cli -run 'TestCandidateApplyV2|TestCandidatePipeline(Blank|LoadsFresh|Force)|TestDistillApplication' -count=1\n```\n\nNo remaining H/M ownership issue in the latest implementation."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a02fb8-5db4-77e3-a158-975075162964"}}}
