{"timestamp":"2026-08-23T18:15:24.067Z","ordinal":18120,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a02fd5-9ea1-7d82-99e1-f79f4d0dcddf","author":"/root/phase3_quality_review","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/phase3_quality_review\nPayload:\nFinal H/M review: no HIGH/MEDIUM blockers found.\n\nThe owned/shared marker logic now handles the preservation edge correctly:\n\n- Pre-existing distilled/authored exact facts receive a `shared` marker.\n- Newly created v2 facts receive an `owned` marker.\n- Shared-only cleanup removes the candidate anchor but preserves the fact, including anchorless legacy facts.\n- Owned facts are deleted only when their last owned v2 anchor is removed.\n- Multiple exact v2 candidates propagate ownership; removing the first preserves the fact, while removing the last removes it.\n- Receipt-present and receiptless crash recovery use the same durable marker logic.\n- Phase 1/legacy anchors remain outside the validated v2 namespaces.\n\nFocused tests and `git diff --check` pass."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a02fb8-5db4-77e3-a158-975075162964"}}}
